column61:
I agree with the comment about overusing macros though. Instead of:<p><pre><code>    #define DbgEnteringState(x)                                                    \n        printf (&quot;[%s] Unit entering state %s
&quot;, unit->name, #x);
</code></pre>
How about:<p><pre><code>    static void dbg_entering_state(unit_t * unit, const char * state_name) {
        fprintf (stderr, &quot;[%s] Unit entering state %s
&quot;, unit->name, state_name);
    }
</code></pre>
Friendlier to humans reading code, IDEs, and debuggers. I went ahead and fixed it writing to the wrong stdio stream too.
